WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.791 --> 00:00:02.923
(audience cheering)
- Oh my God!

00:00:02.923 --> 00:00:05.763
I know, get it out,
get it out, get it out!

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:12.173
I've never seen the band
clapping this hard! (laughs)

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.790
This is the first time
in four seasons I look up

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.730
and they're like, Yeah, woo! (claps)

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.590
So wait, I hear you came with a request

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.850
of some sort, did you?

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.580
- Oh, he is a Hamilton super-fan,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.641
- I am, we all are.

00:00:25.641 --> 00:00:26.542
- And especially-
- Who isn't?

00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:28.170
- Your rendition of "It's Quiet Uptown."

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.020
- Well, that's nice!
- He sings it often.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.536
- That's your favorite?
- That's my favorite.

00:00:33.536 --> 00:00:34.369
- That's a sad song, man!

00:00:34.369 --> 00:00:36.210
- It puts me into a relaxing stage,

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.464
it makes me appreciate life.

00:00:38.464 --> 00:00:42.570
- Oh, an optimist! Cause
that's a dark song.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.850
- Yeah, I try to take the
positives out of the darkness.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.345
- You do.

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:49.873
If that's what you see in that
song, you are an optimist.

00:00:49.873 --> 00:00:51.087
(all laugh)
- Thank you.

00:00:51.087 --> 00:00:52.497
- I was pregnant with my
son when I had to sing that

00:00:52.497 --> 00:00:55.202
and I hadn't seen Hamilton
yet and I was like,

00:00:55.202 --> 00:00:57.240
(mock sobbing) it was just
the saddest thing ever.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.040
But God, what a great musical.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.800
You saw it obviously,
right? Like how many times?

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.480
- We're super-fans.
- I know, me too.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.948
- It's a problem.

00:01:04.948 --> 00:01:06.250
- We corner Lin when we see him.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.083
(Kelly laughs)
Tell us more.

00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:08.790
- I corner him, make
him show up at my show.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.320
I'm like, Please come back, I love you.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.286
So wait, you recently celebrated,

00:01:12.286 --> 00:01:13.343
is it your eighth anniversary?

00:01:13.343 --> 00:01:14.176
- (in unison) Yeah.

00:01:14.176 --> 00:01:16.117
- That's amazing!
(audience applauds)

00:01:16.117 --> 00:01:19.050
I heard there's something
called the Wade World Tour.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.633
What is this and how do you get invited?

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.933
(audience laughs)
- You gotta be fun!

00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:28.440
We celebrate our anniversary

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.530
with several other couple friends-

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.530
- Oh, just got disinvited, okay. (laughs)

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.330
- There's still time, we're
both on marriage number two.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.080
So, still time.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.270
We celebrate together, we all
celebrate our anniversaries

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:44.130
and we figure out ways of
loving each other better.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:47.067
- [Kelly] That's awesome! You
all do it together on a trip?

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.398
(audience applauds)
- [Gabrielle and Dwayne] Yeah.

00:01:48.398 --> 00:01:50.760
- [Kelly] That's really fun! Oh my God!

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.190
So that's a yacht, okay.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.690
- Yeah, that's us working
on our relationship.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.216
- We like to travel.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:58.290
- I'm like, usually people go to therapy,

00:01:58.290 --> 00:01:59.610
y'all go to like, paradise.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.849
- We go and get away from
everybody so it's just us.

00:02:01.849 --> 00:02:03.398
- [Kelly] It's smart.

00:02:03.398 --> 00:02:05.160
- [Dwayne] It's just us 12,
we gotta deal with it all.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.587
Did y'all see that?
(audience cheers)

00:02:07.587 --> 00:02:11.010
- And you enjoy each other in
a dating capacity, probably.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.450
That's romantic, that's nice.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.310
- Well it's like you kind
of meet each other again,

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.260
away from kids, away from work,

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.420
out in the middle of nowhere,

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.760
and you gotta kind of figure
out how to love each other

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.080
and like each other better.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.113
- What have been your favorite
stops on the Wade World Tour?

00:02:26.236 --> 00:02:27.390
- One of my favorite stops was,

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.600
we were in the South of France, as one is-

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.516
- That's nice, I've been there.

00:02:32.516 --> 00:02:33.349
- We're obsessed.

00:02:33.349 --> 00:02:34.410
And we were going to this place for lunch

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:38.134
and they were like, Oh my gosh,
Elton John is always there.

00:02:38.134 --> 00:02:39.600
- Shout out to Pecos, our friend.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.740
- Yeah, our friend Pecos.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.050
He's like, Elton John's always
there and he's always singing

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.606
and we're like, That's not
gonna happen when we go.

00:02:45.606 --> 00:02:47.756
- What? Didn't happen
when I went anywhere.

00:02:49.228 --> 00:02:50.310
- And who's there?
- [Kelly] No way!

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.593
- Elton John.
(audience applauds)

00:02:53.593 --> 00:02:57.210
Cut to, you hear the first chords

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.730
of all of your favorite Elton John songs

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.380
and he's like, No I could never!

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.430
And he stands up and proceeds
to do a full concert.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:07.800
The whole place goes nuts.
- Legendary.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.720
- It was unbelievable.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.820
- That's so crazy!

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.400
- What's your favorite,
though? Your favorite memory.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.663
- Oh, my favorite memory?

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.200
- Or like, place to go if
y'all go different places.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.103
- Calvin Harris?

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.040
- Well yes, this year we was in Spain

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.540
and we got an opportunity in Ibiza

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.574
to see Calvin Harris.

00:03:26.574 --> 00:03:28.286
- I really wanna be a part of your lives.

00:03:28.286 --> 00:03:30.888
So like wait, what? I'm doing
something wrong. (laughs)

00:03:30.888 --> 00:03:31.895
(audience claps)

00:03:31.895 --> 00:03:35.340
- You see, Calvin Harris and
the way he controls the crowd

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.712
is amazing.

00:03:36.712 --> 00:03:39.274
I've heard a lot of great things about him

00:03:39.274 --> 00:03:40.200
and first time being at the show,

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:43.770
it was raining, it was
thunder, it was lightning.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:45.690
It was everything that you can ask for

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.770
and Calvin Harris was doing his thing.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.510
So I was out there, shirt
off, just like ah! Screaming.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:52.343
It was amazing.

00:03:53.178 --> 00:03:54.450
- Oh, that's such a great feeling,

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.620
being lost in music like that.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.240
I feel like we missed
that for a couple years

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.280
cause we weren't really allowed to gather.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.500
God, it's like you get
drunk off that energy now.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.886
- Or drunk off other things.
- [Kelly] Yes, or...(laughs)

00:04:05.886 --> 00:04:07.680
A good time with help.
(audience clapping)

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.284
- It was Ibiza.

00:04:09.284 --> 00:04:10.834
There might have been
something in the air.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:11.894
- [Kelly] There's songs about it.

00:04:11.894 --> 00:04:12.727
- Some herbal essence in the air.

00:04:12.727 --> 00:04:14.220
But we were so into it,

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.760
cause we never really do the Deuce Deuce,

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.480
we're more of, Kelly Clarkson,
Patti LaBelle, Beyonce.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.743
- Can I just, wow! I love
the company, thank you!

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.740
I don't belong in that
sentence, but I like it.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.201
- So we don't know.

00:04:30.201 --> 00:04:31.440
So we see this plane go over, we're like,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.770
Oh yo, they're pulling out all the stops!

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:36.240
We think this is a part of the show.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.330
It starts raining, the wind,
there's actual lightning.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.635
We're in danger, we're like, Oh!

00:04:41.635 --> 00:04:43.504
- This is amazing.
- This is amazing!

00:04:43.504 --> 00:04:45.965
The production value is really top-notch.

00:04:45.965 --> 00:04:47.190
- It's probably that herbal thing.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:49.272
You're like, This is awesome!

00:04:49.272 --> 00:04:51.159
- Everyone's leaving, we like,
What are they leaving for?

00:04:51.159 --> 00:04:52.646
This is great!
- This is the best!

00:04:52.646 --> 00:04:54.241
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:54.241 --> 00:04:55.074
Like Dwayne Wade died today.

00:04:55.074 --> 00:04:56.549
- I wanna go on vacation
with y'all just to watch.

00:04:56.549 --> 00:04:57.382
(audience applauds)

00:04:57.382 --> 00:04:58.891
- So has it been nice
to have Dwayne at home

00:04:58.891 --> 00:05:01.213
since retiring, is that nice? (laughs)

00:05:03.052 --> 00:05:04.680
- It has gotten nice.
(audience laughs)

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:09.660
Initially, our careers
were on opposite coasts

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.520
so we were never really home together

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.200
for long stretches of time.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.257
So it would be like, every
morning, Oh! There you are.

00:05:16.257 --> 00:05:20.700
(Kelly laughs)
Look at his face!

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:22.172
Over time, it's awesome.

00:05:22.172 --> 00:05:23.905
- [Kelly] It's probably
weird for you, too!

00:05:23.905 --> 00:05:26.343
- Thank you. No one ever
asks me, Is it weird?

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.070
- You know why? Cause
that's like musicians,

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:30.900
we're on the road all the time

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:31.740
and that can be hard in a relationship.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:35.280
Then you try and almost put
yourself in this situation,

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:37.080
the family's already kind
of doing its own thing

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.630
while you've been gone, so that's hard.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.340
- Yes, so I just had to be quiet

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.055
for like the first six months.

00:05:43.055 --> 00:05:45.133
- (laughs) Good job, that's hard.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:46.788
- Yeah, just shut up and listen.

00:05:46.788 --> 00:05:48.663
I've found my space now in the house.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:54.686
The rent I pay, I feel like
I'm getting my money's worth.

00:05:54.686 --> 00:05:56.692
- (laughs and claps)
I'm a part, I'm a part.

00:05:56.692 --> 00:05:59.658
- [Dwayne] Get my money's worth.

00:05:59.658 --> 00:06:01.996
- You've been married for eight years,

00:06:01.996 --> 00:06:03.240
so is there anything that drives you nuts,

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.130
I know there's something
that drives you nuts,

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:05.963
about the other person?

00:06:05.963 --> 00:06:08.112
- We gotta pick one thing, or...?

00:06:08.112 --> 00:06:10.500
- (laughs) I got a list.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.400
- He acts like there's the
Dead Sea Scrolls of complaints.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:18.390
- All the guys in here,
what's up, how y'all doing?

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:20.237
So can I go first?

00:06:20.237 --> 00:06:21.780
- I just wanna steal that! (laughs)

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:25.072
Dead Sea Scrolls of complaints! Go ahead.

00:06:25.072 --> 00:06:28.500
- So my wife stopped
driving a few years ago.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.080
She got into a few fender-benders...

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:32.940
- Maybe realized it wasn't your thing.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:33.773
- [Gabrielle] Not my thing.

00:06:33.773 --> 00:06:38.460
- So it wasn't her thing and
I was all for it, so I drive.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:39.810
When she gets in the passenger seat,

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:44.810
she tells me how to drive,
all the time. All the time.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:48.510
She never drives but she
tells me how to drive.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.830
- You're my sister.

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:51.840
Every time we're in the car
with she and Sean, her husband,

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.910
I'm like, Lisa, let him drive!

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:55.260
She's always got something to say

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.910
and I'm like, Why don't you drive?

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.060
That's you! That's you.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.590
- I was going 20 miles
an hour the other day,

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:02.690
she's like, Slow down!

00:07:03.525 --> 00:07:04.500
- We were in a school zone.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.020
We rarely get to do the drop-off,

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.880
our youngest daughter's drop-off,

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.970
and I just felt like it was
Mario Andretti out there.

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:13.593
I'm like, Pump the brakes, sir!

00:07:14.623 --> 00:07:16.110
- (laughing) You are my sister!

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:18.210
- It felt faster than he was...

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:20.445
I think it's my turn though, hold on.

00:07:20.445 --> 00:07:21.510
(audience laughs)

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:24.493
- I was hoping like the
time ran, like commercial.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:30.510
- He snores, he is a snorer.
- If I'm on my back.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.760
- He knows he snores.
(audience laughs)

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:33.593
- If I'm on my back!

00:07:33.593 --> 00:07:35.760
- If you know you snore
on your back, turn over.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.080
- You can't control that in your sleep.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.420
- Thank you.
- That's what he thinks.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:42.960
- It's only because age
hit and I started snoring

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:45.270
and I was like, This is not hot.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.920
- I didn't know we was coming
to therapy, this is great.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.189
Thank you, Kelly.

00:07:48.189 --> 00:07:50.375
- But it's not just enough that he snores,

00:07:50.375 --> 00:07:53.520
he brings our dog, Trey,
who's a little Frenchie.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.348
His little nose is like this
big and they snore together.

00:07:57.348 --> 00:07:59.101
(audience exclaims)
- Oh no.

00:07:59.101 --> 00:08:01.050
- It's like a symphony of snoring

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:03.030
and Trey is very territorial.

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:04.593
He's like, That's my man, girl.

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:08.790
He always has to be in-between us

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.310
and normally, when it was
just him in bed snoring,

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:12.600
I would just give him
a little rabbit punch

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:13.904
and he was like, What, what?

00:08:13.904 --> 00:08:15.664
And I'm like, I don't
know, something happened.

00:08:15.664 --> 00:08:17.553
(Kelly laughs)
And that would stop.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.120
So last night, he brought the dog in

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.210
and he forgot to take him
out and I'm petting Trey,

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:25.950
I'm like, Oh baby, did you have a big day?

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:28.710
Next thing I know, he's peed on my feet.

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:30.450
And I'm like, Baby!

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.780
So before we even got to
the snoring, there was dog-

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:34.613
- [Kelly] Pee.

00:08:34.613 --> 00:08:35.730
And that sucks when you're tired.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:37.080
That's happened to me too, we have a puppy

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.040
in our house right now and you're like,

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.690
Oh cool, I'll just go ahead
and change all the sheets

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:42.960
right now at 10:30, that's nice. (laughs)

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.850
I wasn't tired or anything, it's fine.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:48.000
So your youngest daughter
is almost four now

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.100
and she's quite the dancer.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:52.080
Everybody take a look at this.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:53.603
- [Gabrielle] I love this!

00:08:53.603 --> 00:08:54.540
(audience awwing)

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:58.293
- [Kelly] Look, she is so focused!

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.680
- [Dwayne] She's serious.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:04.110
- [Kelly] This is my daughter
at dance, by the way.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.850
Yeah, she is so focused.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:08.520
- [Dwayne] We give pep
talks, before we go in.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.180
- Are y'all those parents like,
Baby smile? Are you those?

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:14.063
- It's like when she look at, Smile!

00:09:15.194 --> 00:09:17.430
- I just feel like we put a lot of work in

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:20.038
and it's time to deliver, you know?

00:09:20.038 --> 00:09:21.150
(audience laughing)

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:22.170
- It's time to deliver.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:23.700
- [Gabrielle] It's time to deliver.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:27.458
Not unlike me, how I was at
his games, where I was like,

00:09:27.458 --> 00:09:28.823
Let's go, three! Let's go, three!

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:33.183
Come on now, free throws are
free for a reason, let's go!

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.430
So perhaps I'm not the best dance mom.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.263
- [Kelly] Oh my God!

00:09:40.263 --> 00:09:43.290
- I just say to Kaav, I
just say, That's your mom.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.090
Kaav try to look at me
cause mom is over here,

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:47.550
I'll be like...
- [Kelly] Look at me.

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:49.440
- Focus on me.
- Calm.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.640
- She's a little stressed.
- She's excited.

00:09:53.187 --> 00:09:54.437
- So Kaav focuses on dad.

00:09:55.427 --> 00:09:56.260
(audience cheering)

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:57.831
- So you two have now created

00:09:57.831 --> 00:09:59.790
a line of baby products called Proudly.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:02.010
What can you tell us about
it and why'd you start it?

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.930
- We created the line because we realized

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:08.280
there was a gross lack
of quality, safe products

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:10.653
that centered the needs
of melanated children,

00:10:11.937 --> 00:10:13.950
and knowing that we have
access to everything

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.500
and we couldn't find it for our child.

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:19.290
We started talking to
other parents of color

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:22.735
and we were all realizing that
our kids were overindexing

00:10:22.735 --> 00:10:25.080
on skin concerns, like
eczema, extreme dryness,

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:28.254
cradle cap, diaper rash, that looked-

00:10:28.254 --> 00:10:30.540
- [Dwayne] It's just dark skin.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:32.787
- Baby acne and our
children were overindexing

00:10:32.787 --> 00:10:35.130
and we realized that even
though there are products

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:36.660
that say "Safe for children,"

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:39.120
they aren't the best
for melanated children.

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:40.470
We have different skin needs

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.270
and we wanted to meet those needs.

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:43.770
- That's amazing.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:46.770
So why did you name it Proudly?

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:48.630
- I think it's just that, right?

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:50.400
We're proud of this brand.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:54.240
We hope that families,
this is gonna be something

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:56.910
that they're gonna be proud
to introduce to their homes.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:59.040
It's hard to introduce new things.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:00.420
We all like things that we like

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:02.400
and our grandparents like,
and our parents like,

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:04.740
but we want them to be proud to introduce

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:06.420
something that we feel that...

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:08.160
Shout out to our
dermatologist out the Beach,

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:13.160
shout out to our pediatrician,
Dr. McGowan, our entire team.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.710
We're proud of the structure
we were able to put together.

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:18.810
We partnered up with A-Frame,
it's an amazing company,

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:20.850
and we said, This is what we
want our team to look like,

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:22.560
this is what we want it to feel like.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:23.700
We want it to look like the people

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:25.350
that we're trying to
make these products for,

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:26.610
and that's what our team looks like.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:31.610
- 90% of our team is women,
95% are people of color.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.390
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:34.410
- Wow, which is important!

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:36.300
- It's important because-
- You're working on a product

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:37.133
that's for the...

00:11:37.133 --> 00:11:37.966
- Oftentimes you'll be like,

00:11:37.966 --> 00:11:40.110
Who designed these
feminine hygiene products,

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:42.300
things that women use, and you're like,

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.610
It's a bunch of dudes!

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:45.443
How do you know about-

00:11:45.443 --> 00:11:47.190
- That's what I say about heels.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:49.490
- Exactly, torture devices.
- That was a man.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:52.473
That was a dumb person's idea.

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:56.430
I'm mad about it still.

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:58.890
And it was invented, I think,
for kings to feel taller.

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:01.530
I'm suffering cause you felt short?

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.180
(audience laughs)
I'm mad about it.

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:04.260
- But that's the thing.

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:06.610
It's like, Who's making these products

00:12:07.448 --> 00:12:11.432
and are you just trying to
exploit people who have needs?

00:12:11.432 --> 00:12:14.790
In creating this company for us, by us,

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.680
by people of color for children of color,

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:19.530
and the majority of the people
that work for us are parents.

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:20.850
So we're creating the products

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:22.623
that we wanna use in our own homes.

00:12:23.674 --> 00:12:27.030
So it creates a very proud, united front.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:28.650
- I love that that's
when it happens though,

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:30.780
it's like something you need
and you want and you desire

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:33.180
and you're like, Look, not
everybody can make this happen.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:34.830
You have the power to
actually make that happen,

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:35.880
not only for yourselves
but for other people.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.410
- The resources.
- You have the resources.

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:39.660
- Yeah, you have the networking,
you have all of that.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:41.010
So it's really awesome for y'all

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:43.020
but also how you're
helping so many others.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:45.600
- The best things come
out of outta need, right?

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:47.730
So to be able to create
a product and a brand

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:50.760
out of something that is
a real need in the world,

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:51.690
we're proud of that.

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:53.910
So the name just kind of, it made itself.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.410
- Yeah, Proudly. That's cool.

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:57.366
- Target was like, what? We want in!

00:12:57.366 --> 00:13:00.122
(audience applauds)
- I love Target.

00:13:00.122 --> 00:13:00.955
- Don't I look like a Proudly parent?

00:13:00.955 --> 00:13:02.780
- It's hard to get in Target!
- It's hard to get in Target.

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:04.808
- [Kelly] I don't know if y'all know that.

00:13:04.808 --> 00:13:05.700
- Shout out to Target.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:07.530
- Immediately they were
like, We want this.

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:09.720
- That's awesome!
- So we're in-

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.180
- That store, you go in for
two things and leave with 50,

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:15.132
and not one was the two
things you went in for.

00:13:15.132 --> 00:13:17.341
(all laugh)

00:13:17.341 --> 00:13:20.370
So is Kaavia, is she a
part of your focus group?

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:21.600
Does she test out your stuff?

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:24.090
- She is the focus group.
- Oh yeah.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:26.700
- If she didn't like it,
we will never see it.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:28.230
- [Kelly] They're so honest about it.

00:13:28.230 --> 00:13:29.645
- [Gabrielle] They're painfully honest.

00:13:29.645 --> 00:13:31.902
- [Dwayne] But she has to
be able to do it herself.

00:13:31.902 --> 00:13:33.493
- [Kelly] Oh, independent!

00:13:33.493 --> 00:13:35.949
- So we had to make sure
that the product was made

00:13:35.949 --> 00:13:39.304
to a point where it was
easy for her to use.

00:13:39.304 --> 00:13:40.365
- For all toddlers to be able to use.

00:13:40.365 --> 00:13:41.198
- The caps and the tops and everything.

00:13:41.198 --> 00:13:42.900
- My little girl loves that.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:45.007
She hates when I have to help her,

00:13:45.007 --> 00:13:47.527
she loves the independence of it.

00:13:47.527 --> 00:13:49.500
- She was getting it, she couldn't use it,

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:52.050
so we had to go back and say,
No, we want a different cap,

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:53.190
we want a different top.

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:56.580
All these things was important
for Kaav to use 'em herself.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:58.110
- But we used our whole family.

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:01.440
Anyone that we knew with
babies, small children,

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.453
everyone became our focus group.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:07.500
I looked down one day
and I was like, Ooh, baby

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.453
those knuckles are ashy!

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.720
- [Kelly] Perhaps not
his finest hour. (laughs)

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:15.543
- [Gabrielle] And I was
like, Well, if this can work,

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:17.860
we're in business.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:19.230
- [Kelly] (laughs) I
love what's happening.

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:23.823
You two, your house
must be so insanely fun.

